Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 15:35:03 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 13/13] radv: no CMASK fast clear for a console display surface

On the PS4 the GPU rendered the preamble, then wedged in the frame body on
both a clear and a draw: RADV had given the swapchain's scanout image a
CMASK and was doing a CMASK fast clear. A console display scans out raw
pixels and nothing resolves the compression on a flip, so the CB never
completed.

A scanout surface on a winsys other than amdgpu gets no single-sample
CMASK, so the clear is a plain one and rendering is uncompressed, as a
display can scan out. DCC, the GFX8+ counterpart, is already disabled for
scanout.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01R3DbSodVLhQVcvZSazbPue
---
 src/amd/vulkan/radv_image.c | 11 ++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/amd/vulkan/radv_image.c b/src/amd/vulkan/radv_image.c
index 05d02b3..3b5fcf0 100644
--- a/src/amd/vulkan/radv_image.c
+++ b/src/amd/vulkan/radv_image.c
@@ -843,10 +843,19 @@ static void
 radv_image_alloc_single_sample_cmask(const struct radv_device *device, const struct radv_image *image,
                                      struct radeon_surf *surf)
 {
+   const struct radv_physical_device *pdev = radv_device_physical(device);
+
    if (!surf->cmask_size || surf->cmask_offset || surf->bpe > 8 || image->vk.mip_levels > 1 ||
        image->vk.extent.depth > 1 || radv_image_has_dcc(image) || !radv_image_use_fast_clear_for_image(device, image) ||
        (image->vk.create_flags & VK_IMAGE_CREATE_2_SPARSE_BINDING_BIT_KHR) ||
-       (image->vk.usage & VK_IMAGE_USAGE_2_HOST_TRANSFER_BIT_KHR))
+       (image->vk.usage & VK_IMAGE_USAGE_2_HOST_TRANSFER_BIT_KHR) ||
+       /* A console display scans out raw pixels, and there is no kernel or
+        * compositor to resolve compression on a flip: a scanout surface gets
+        * no CMASK, so neither a CMASK fast clear nor the compressed rendering
+        * that a fast-clear eliminate would have to resolve (the PS4, whose
+        * GFX7 fast clear is CMASK; DCC, disabled for scanout above, is the
+        * GFX8+ one). The desktop (amdgpu) keeps CMASK. */
+       ((surf->flags & RADEON_SURF_SCANOUT) && !pdev->info.is_amdgpu))
       return;
 
    assert(image->vk.samples == 1);
